{
  "subject": {
    "slug": "radiation-protection",
    "title": "Radiation Protection",
    "order": 9
  },
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "mri-safety",
    "title": "MRI Safety Screening",
    "order": 0,
    "pages": [
      {
        "title": "A Different Kind of Hazard",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "MRI doesn't use ionizing radiation, but the MR environment has its own serious, unique safety hazards \u2014 and as RT departments increasingly use MRI for simulation and treatment planning, screening awareness matters even outside a dedicated MRI department."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "The defining hazard of an MRI suite is its "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "strong static magnetic field, which is always on",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " \u2014 even when the scanner isn't actively imaging. Unlike a LINAC, you can't just walk away from the hazard by leaving the beam off; the magnet's field is a constant, permanent feature of the room."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "The Three-Tier Safety Classification",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Every implant, device, and piece of equipment used in or near the MR environment must be labeled with one of three official classifications:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Label"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Meaning"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "MR Unsafe",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Should never enter the MRI scanner room. Patients with an MR Unsafe device should not be scanned."
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "MR Conditional",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "May safely enter the scanner room "
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "only",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "italic"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": " under the very specific conditions stated in its labeling."
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "MR Safe",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Poses no safety hazard anywhere in the MR environment. No scanning restrictions."
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page2_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A patient has a device labeled \"MR Conditional.\" Is it automatically safe to scan them?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Yes, \"conditional\" just means it's a slightly older safety label",
              "No, only if the device is positively identified as MR Conditional AND its specific conditions for safe use are actually met"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "\"Conditional\" means safe only under specific, verified conditions \u2014 never assume it's safe without confirming the exact conditions are met for that specific scanner."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "What \"Conditional\" Actually Means",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "For a device "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "intended to enter the bore",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " of the MRI system, its labeling must be matched against the specific scanner being used, checking:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Static field strength",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " (e.g., is this rated for 1.5T, 3T?)"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Maximum spatial field gradient",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "dB/dt limitations",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " (usually only relevant for active implants like pacemakers)"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "SAR limits",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " (Specific Absorption Rate \u2014 RF energy deposition)"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Any other device-specific conditions, such as restrictions on which coils may be used"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Expected temperature rise and imaging artifact extent may also be listed \u2014 these inform the risk/benefit decision but are "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "not",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " pass/fail conditions the way the items above are."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Equipment That Stays Outside the Bore",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Items "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "not intended to enter the bore",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " \u2014 like most ancillary room equipment \u2014 are conditional in a different way: they typically carry "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "gauss line positioning restrictions",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " (must stay outside a specified field-strength boundary) or must be "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "tethered or affixed",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " to an immovable part of the room."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "This is why oxygen tanks, IV poles, and other equipment brought into an MR suite must be MR-rated versions specifically, not just \"whatever was in the supply closet.\" A standard ferromagnetic oxygen tank becomes a dangerous projectile in a strong magnetic field \u2014 this is called the "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "missile effect",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": ", and it's the signature hazard unique to the MR environment."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Screening Patients \u2014 Implants and Foreign Bodies",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Before any patient enters the MR environment, screening covers several categories:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Biomedical implants",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 pacemakers, defibrillators, aneurysm clips, cochlear implants, neurostimulators. Many modern devices are MR Conditional, but this must be verified per-device, never assumed."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Ferrous foreign bodies",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 metal shavings or fragments (a real concern for patients with a occupational metalworking history), shrapnel. Ocular metal fragments are a particular concern given proximity to the eye."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Screening Patients \u2014 Conditions and External Items",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Medical conditions",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 pregnancy is specifically screened for and factors into the risk/benefit discussion"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Prior diagnostic or surgical procedures",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 surgical hardware, clips, or stents from past procedures may not be documented in the chart the technologist has access to"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Topical or externally applied items",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 tattoos (some pigments contain metallic compounds), medication patches (may have a metallic backing), body piercings, monitoring devices, and clothing with metal components (zippers, underwire)"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page6_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A patient has a medication patch. Why does this matter for MRI screening?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "It has no relevance to MRI safety",
              "Some patches have a metallic backing that can heat up or cause a burn in the MR field"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Metallic-backed patches can heat significantly during scanning, posing a real burn risk \u2014 this is exactly why \"topical or externally applied items\" is its own screening category."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Ancillary Equipment in the MR Suite",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Beyond the patient, everything else brought into the scanner room needs the same scrutiny: oxygen tanks, IV poles, monitoring equipment, wheelchairs, and stretchers. All of these need MR-safe or MR-conditional versions specifically designed for the MR environment \u2014 a standard hospital wheelchair is a serious missile-effect hazard."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "The RTT's Role",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Even in a radiation therapy department that primarily uses MRI for simulation and fusion rather than diagnostic imaging, the same screening discipline applies every time a patient or piece of equipment approaches the scanner. When in doubt about a device's classification, the answer is always to verify against its actual labeling \u2014 never assume based on appearance, general device category, or what a similar-looking device was rated for."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Wrap-up:",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " you've covered the three-tier MR Safe/Conditional/Unsafe classification system, what \"conditional\" requires for bore vs. non-bore equipment, the missile effect, and the categories of patient and equipment screening."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
